.TH CVEC_CONSTRUCT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvec_construct \- type-safe vector construction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cvector.h>

cvec_construct(vec_name, type);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-safe macro for creating a vector. Automatically determines element
size from the type and creates a type marker variable that lets the
other type-dispatching macros know the declared element type at each
call site.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
vec_name  Name of the vector variable to create
type      Element type (e.g., int, double, struct foo)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Terminates program on allocation failure
Creates a hidden type marker variable that the other type-dispatching
macros read; cvec_redeclare(3) recreates it in another scope
Equivalent to cvector_create(sizeof(type), &err) with error handling
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cvec_construct(my_vec, int);
cvec_push_rvalue(my_vec, 42);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_construct_scoped (3),
.BR cvector_create (3)
